 open problem.\n\nantichain crystallographic dyck path poset rational dyck path root poset root system simplicial complex\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the rate of convergence of continued fraction statistics of random rationals | Selecta Mathematica | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00029-025-01026-9)\nciteturn2search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; We show that the statistics of the continued fraction expansion of a randomly chosen rational in the unit interval, with a fixed large denominator q, approaches the Gauss-Kuzmin statistics with polynomial rate in q.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[Revue de papier] Toeplitz Unlabeled Sensing (https://www.themoonlight.io/fr/review/toeplitz-unlabeled-sensing)\nciteturn2search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Based on Theorem 1, the paper derives the Toeplitz unlabeled sensing theorem, Theorem 2.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPapers from 2026-10-28 - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/date/2026-10-28)\nciteturn2search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 days ago; Crawled: today; We determine the bigraded Frobenius series of the superspace coinvariant ring $R^{(1,1)}_{\\mathbb{Z}_r\\wr\\mathfrak{S}_n}$ for the wreath products $\\mathbb{Z}_r\\wr\\mathfrak{S}_n$, which is the quotient of the ring $\\mathbb{C}[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]\\otimes\\bigwedge[θ_1,\\ldots,θ_n]$ of polynomial-valued differential forms by the ideal generated by diagonal $\\mathbb{Z}_r\\wr\\mathfrak{S}_n$-invariants with vanishing constant term. ... In 2026, Francisco Santos presented a question of Juan Benigno Seoane-Sepúlveda on the existence of all-even sets in dimensions $3$ and higher, together with examples of such sets in dimension $2$. ... This confirms a conjecture posed by Lang and Sanhueza-Matama